,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],"stderr":[],"exit_code":0,"match_count":76,"file_matches":[{"path":"/Users/kimhawk/.agents/skills/h-mad/SKILL.md","matches":[{"line_number":3,"content":"description: \"Orchestrate the seven-phase H-MAD development workflow end to end with project invariants, independent audits, test-first implementation, verification, and closure. Use for /h-mad feature, /h-mad do feature, /h-mad status, or /h-mad reset feature.\""},{"line_number":8,"content":"## Host runtime"},{"line_number":22,"content":"## Activation surface"},{"line_number":28,"content":"| `/h-mad status [<feature>]` | Auto-bootstrap if needed. Read-only. Print state from `docs/.bkit-memory.json`. Surface stale `phase = \"step5\"` flags (heuristic: `autonomous_entry_ts > 60min` ago AND `halt_reason = null`). |"},{"line_number":32,"content":"## First-run auto-bootstrap"},{"line_number":66,"content":"— **except under `/h-mad status`, which is documented read-only and must stay so.** Item 3 writes"},{"line_number":67,"content":"under `~/.claude/agents/`, i.e. outside the project entirely, so firing it from a read-only verb"},{"line_number":68,"content":"widens that verb's blast radius into the user's home config. Under `status`, report item 3 as unmet"},{"line_number":166,"content":"## Bootstrap action"},{"line_number":226,"content":"## Decision routing (for `/h-mad \"<feature>\"`)"},{"line_number":283,"content":"`halt_reason` that outlived its resolution by four hours and eight shipped"},{"line_number":284,"content":"modules, and a `last_completed_phase` still reading 4 after Phase 5 had merged"},{"line_number":301,"content":"| `halted` | **Run the staleness check first** (below) — a halt that commits landed after is usually already resolved. Then print `halt_reason` + recovery hints (see `references/failure-recovery.md`). Ask \"resume, retry, or reset?\" |"},{"line_number":304,"content":"## Per-phase actions"},{"line_number":323,"content":"## Phase 5 (Implementation) sub-steps"},{"line_number":374,"content":"  coexisting plugins. A FAIL therefore cannot be detected by exit status, and"},{"line_number":463,"content":"- **5e** — GREEN dispatch (`references/codex-implementer-prompt.md` + `references/agy-spec-reviewer-prompt.md`). **Stage the Codex half with `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py --phase green`** (the agy spec-review half is still assembled by hand). Note the sandbox rule it enforces for you: never dispatch a pytest-running phase with `--sandbox read-only` — it kills pytest's tempdir, so the run passes without measuring anything. The same applies to the anti-gaming verifier dispatch below, which the assembler does not yet stage. **Transport: default `hmad-dispatch exec` for a one-shot GREEN + its review** (§\"Exit-code dispatch for 5d/5e\"); use the pane path (`send`) for the iterative revision loop where cycles 2..N reuse the warm thread — there the alive-check + context-clear below apply. For the pane path: re-verify the Codex + agy panes alive and **clear each pane's context** (§\"Agent-pane context hygiene\") before the first GREEN dispatch of a feature. For each module, dispatch Codex for implementa [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":489,"content":"- **5f** — **Derive the 5c sha, never `git merge-base`.** `python3 ~/.claude/skills/h-mad/scripts/h_mad_baseline_sha.py --branch <feature-branch> [--trunk main]`, reading the `BASELINE:` token, never `$?`. 5c is `git checkout -b …; commit impl-plan + audit files`, so the 5c commit is the branch's FIRST commit and `git merge-base main <branch>` returns the commit it forked FROM — off by exactly the impl-plan commit, and off plausibly, since both are real shas on the right branch. Measured (J41): merge-base `b5c8f41` against real 5c `730cc16`, 313 lines apart — the impl-plan and its three audits, which the wrong base feeds into the review as newly-added content when they are a separate INPUT to it. `UNVERIFIED` is a verdict, not an error: the branch's first commit does not touch an impl-plan, so something was committed before 5c and the rule does not hold — find the commit by hand, and note the token reports it as `candidate=` rather than `sha=` precisely so an unvouched value cannot be  [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":494,"content":"  **Run the mutations through `h_mad_mutation_harness.py` rather than by hand.** `python3 ~/.claude/skills/h-mad/scripts/h_mad_mutation_harness.py <spec.json>`, where the spec names the suite command and each mutation as an exact `find`/`replace`. Read the `MUTATION:` token, never `$?`. The harness exists because the hard part of this pass is not choosing mutations, it is proving each one **landed**: an anchor that matches zero times mutates nothing, the suite stays green, and the run reports the guard as enforced — the failure `invariants.base.md` §\"Mutation verification\" names, and one every hand-rolled harness has to re-derive. It refuses any anchor not found exactly once — printing `hint:` lines with the near-miss line numbers, so a drifted anchor no longer costs a manual re-grep — restores the tree on every path including an interrupt, and re-runs the suite afterwards to prove the restore landed. The mutation run performs the sibling sweep itself before the baseline command and re [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":513,"content":"  `codex-authorship`. Record `codex_status=exhausted` or `unavailable` with"},{"line_number":514,"content":"  `h_mad_state_write.py --feature <feat> --set codex_status=exhausted <state_file>`,"},{"line_number":652,"content":"  status line, or to decide whether to keep waiting. Then one poll per 30–60s is right,"},{"line_number":748,"content":"   running `sleep 2; exit 9` reported `{\"satisfied\":true,\"status\":\"exited\",\"exitCode\":0}`."},{"line_number":845,"content":"2. **`git status` / `git diff`** — enumerate what actually landed. Artifacts present with"},{"line_number":942,"content":"## Phase 5 parallel fanout (Orca only)"},{"line_number":991,"content":"## Phase 6 (Verification) sub-steps"},{"line_number":993,"content":"- **6a-prime** — architectural review via agy (`references/agy-architectural-reviewer-prompt.md`). Inputs: Phase 5 diff (BASE = 5c sha; HEAD = 5g sha) + audited design. **Derive the 5c sha, never `git merge-base`.** `python3 ~/.claude/skills/h-mad/scripts/h_mad_baseline_sha.py --branch <feature-branch> [--trunk main]`, reading the `BASELINE:` token, never `$?`. 5c is `git checkout -b …; commit impl-plan + audit files`, so the 5c commit is the branch's FIRST commit and `git merge-base main <branch>` returns the commit it forked FROM — off by exactly the impl-plan commit, and off plausibly, since both are real shas on the right branch. Measured (J41): merge-base `b5c8f41` against real 5c `730cc16`, 313 lines apart — the impl-plan and its three audits, which the wrong base feeds into the review as newly-added content when they are a separate INPUT to it. `UNVERIFIED` is a verdict, not an error: the branch's first commit does not touch an impl-plan, so something was committed before 5c and [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":1009,"content":"## `exec` bounds itself even when you omit `--timeout`"},{"line_number":1039,"content":"## Reading a dispatch verdict"},{"line_number":1114,"content":"If you bypass the wrapper and scrape a pane read-only with the raw CLI"},{"line_number":1133,"content":"## Verifying a review finding before acting on it"},{"line_number":1228,"content":"## Teammate authors — one author, one document, fresh context every time"},{"line_number":1426,"content":"verdict line on purpose**: those spans hold shell metacharacters or a verb outside the read-only"},{"line_number":1437,"content":"explicitly TAGGED, and nothing in a diff hunk is. A span is run only when it is a bare read-only verb"},{"line_number":1736,"content":"## Finding class — build vs measurement"},{"line_number":1779,"content":"## Document-audit round cap — Phase 5 is the gate"},{"line_number":1883,"content":"## Never gate on one audit pass"},{"line_number":1928,"content":"## An agent's reported numbers are a claim, not a measurement"},{"line_number":1949,"content":"## Re-measure a carried premise before working it"},{"line_number":1971,"content":"## Reviewing a skill with agy"},{"line_number":2009,"content":"## Orchestrator context hygiene (your own window)"},{"line_number":2160,"content":"## `hooks/memory-index-guard.sh` — the auto-memory cap, surfaced without being asked"},{"line_number":2219,"content":"## Run-context ceiling — halt the run at 80%"},{"line_number":2287,"content":"## Agent-pane context hygiene"},{"line_number":2328,"content":"## Halt protocol"},{"line_number":2332,"content":"1. Write `orchestrator_state[<feature>]`: `halt_reason = \"<phase>:<sub-step>:<description>\"`, `halt_ts = <now>`, `phase = null`. Pin `current_phase` + `last_completed_phase`."},{"line_number":2338,"content":"## What you NEVER do"},{"line_number":2376,"content":"## Editing this skill while a run is in flight"},{"line_number":2401,"content":"## Confirming a suspected defect before fixing it"},{"line_number":2418,"content":"## Filing to a public tracker"},{"line_number":2429,"content":"## Known interactions (coexisting plugins)"},{"line_number":2448,"content":"## State schema"},{"line_number":2478,"content":"  --feature <feature> --set last_completed_phase=5 --set current_phase=6"},{"line_number":2483,"content":"`halt_reason=step5d:red_not_all_failing` stays a string. A rejected write exits"},{"line_number":2523,"content":"## Audit prompt assembly"},{"line_number":2577,"content":"reads; it does not write. `git status --short` before and after a cycle should be identical, and a"},{"line_number":2597,"content":"It prints `ASSEMBLE: PASS <path> <size> sentinel=<s> size_status=verified|unverified` or"},{"line_number":2610,"content":"**Read `size_status=` on the same line, not just the token.** `verified` means the prompt"},{"line_number":2612,"content":"`references/agent-substrate.md`). `size_status=unverified` still dispatches, because"},{"line_number":2728,"content":"   **Never gate an audit on the dispatch's `result.status`.** The report file and its `.done` marker are the delivery contract; `status` is not. ANY failed or refused tool call yields `status: ERROR` beside a complete, correct answer, and the cause is usually incidental to the audit — measured three times with three unrelated causes: a refused `.tmp` write (`grounding-evidence-coverage` impl-plan cycle 22 pass B, on a report carrying two independently-verified real findings), a `find_by_name` timeout plus a `view_file` on a nonexistent path (2026-08-24, 31 tool calls / 29 ok, schema-correct report), and a `write_to_file` rejected for a missing argument that the agent immediately retried successfully (2026-08-24). This is the same rule `h_mad_review_evidence.py` follows for 6a-prime (step 6a-prime above): report `result.status`, never gate on it. Read the file and the marker."},{"line_number":2788,"content":"## Putting `hmad-dispatch` on PATH"},{"line_number":2799,"content":"## Second surface — the codex leg"},{"line_number":2849,"content":"## Teammate audit leg — when codex is unavailable"},{"line_number":2851,"content":"If `codex_status` records Codex unavailable and `fallback_agent=grok`, prefer"},{"line_number":2865,"content":"`codex_status` declaration:"},{"line_number":2869,"content":"  --feature <feature> --set codex_status=exhausted        # available|unavailable|exhausted"},{"line_number":2951,"content":"  TDD gate hook (`hooks/h-mad-tdd-gate.sh`) reads the **same** `codex_status` for whichever feature"},{"line_number":2972,"content":"## Helper scripts (all in `~/.claude/skills/h-mad/scripts/`)"},{"line_number":2982,"content":"- `h_mad_delta_review.py` — delta self-review over a revision's ADDED lines (#11/H4): `is_command_shaped()` / `is_executable()` / `added_lines()` / `claims()` + CLI printing one `DELTA: CLEAN|CLAIMS|UNREADABLE claims=N executed=E unverified=U` line, a `executed:`/`unverified:` line per claim with the source line, then the `[H-MAD]` marker. Exit 0 on a verdict, 2 on a cannot-judge. Executes only a bare read-only verb with no shell metacharacters, matched on the VERB and never as a substring; everything else is `unverified` and counted. Stdlib-only."},{"line_number":2989,"content":"- `h_mad_assemble_tdd.py` — Phase-5d/5e Codex dispatch assembler: `assemble()` / `task_body()` + CLI printing `ASSEMBLE-TDD: PASS <promptfile> <bytes>B phase=<red|green> task=<id> shape=<s>` followed by the verbatim command block (backgrounded `exec codex` with `--model`/`--effort`/`--out`/`--log`/`--timeout` → `progress` → `h_mad_extract_verdict.py --key STATUS` → an INDEPENDENT scoped pytest), exit 0 on PASS / 2 on `ASSEMBLE-TDD: HALT <reason>`. It stages the prompt and prints the commands; **it does not dispatch** — the dispatch/poll/wait loop is §\"Exit-code dispatch for 5d/5e\", and a driver that dispatches either blocks blind for the timeout or re-implements `progress`. Cuts §\"Task N\" out of the impl-plan using the wire-pin gate's own `_TASK_RE`/`_parse_tasks` rather than a second parser (#39), and stamps the phase into the task section because the template carries BOTH the RED and the GREEN instructions and nothing in it says which applies. Halt reasons: `task_not_found`, `impl_pl [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":2992,"content":"- `h_mad_pane_janitor.py` — post-probe pane cleanup: `snapshot` / `plan` / `clean` + CLI printing `JANITOR: PLANNED|CLEANED|NOTHING|SNAPSHOT candidates=N settled=J closed=K skipped=S` or `JANITOR: REFUSED reason=<r>`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 on a refusal. **Dry run unless `--apply`.** Refusal reasons: `cannot_identify_self`, `baseline_unreadable`, `baseline_malformed`, `too_many_candidates`, `orca_unavailable`, `orca_unparseable`, `orca_error`. The hard part is not closing panes, it is deciding which panes are the probe's: `worker-start` panes inherit the worktree name as their title, so they are indistinguishable from the operator's own agent pane, and each of the seven hand-runs re-typed the keep-list from memory. So take a `snapshot --worktree <path> --out <f>` BEFORE the probe and the keep-list is recorded rather than remembered; a candidate is then a pane in that worktree, absent from the baseline, and not the caller's own — the caller's handle is re-read live from `orca terminal  [... truncated (1031 chars total)]"},{"line_number":3051,"content":"- `h_mad_review_evidence.py` — 6a-prime evidence gate: `scan()` + CLI printing `EVIDENCE: PASS|NONE tools=N ok=K failed=J thinking=T [status=…]`, exit 0 on a verdict / 2 on `EVIDENCE: UNREADABLE reason=no_log|empty_log|unsupported_format`, which carries **no counts** so a cannot-judge cannot read as a zero. Answers only \"did the review read anything\" — never whether its findings are right. Counts any tool reaching `DONE`, knows no tool names, and reports `result.status` without gating on it. `thinking=` sums `usage.thinking_tokens` over completed `agent_response` steps and is reported for the same reason `status` is — triage, never a verdict (J49). Stdlib-only."},{"line_number":3069,"content":"## Git hooks (in `~/.claude/skills/h-mad/git-hooks/`)"},{"line_number":3109,"content":"## Working a `skill-monitoring` item"},{"line_number":3137,"content":"## Telemetry"},{"line_number":3204,"content":"## References"}]}]},"locations":[]}
